"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2980,"Narrated to us Yunus bin Abd al-A'la al-Sadafi; he informed us Ibn Wahb; he informed me Amr bin al-Harith, that Qatada bin Di'ama informed him, on the authority of Anas bin Malik (RA), that he narrated to him: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed the Zuhr and Asr prayers, then the Maghrib and Isha prayers, then took a nap at al-Muhassab, then mounted (his riding animal) and proceeded to the House (the Kaaba), then circumambulated it.""
Abu Bakr said: This is a Gharib Basri hadith, which no one narrated except Amr bin al-Harith. Abu Bakr said: Abu Musa recited this hadith to me, and he stated: Ahmad bin Salih wrote to me (this narration) from Ibn Wahb."
